# Cursor rules — materials

Read AGENTS.md, .agents/STATE.json, .agents/ACTIVE_PLAN.md and .agents/RULES.md before work.
Resume an active checklist step after checking current files; do not repeat completed work.
Maintain [x] completed, [/] active and [ ] pending. Update state after verification.
The session log .agents/history/agent-session-log.md is strictly append-only.

Stack: TypeScript + Next.js App Router + React, Node.js 22+, pnpm 11.25.0.
Application runtime, normal contents maintenance and site verification require no Python.
Python educational notes remain; the removed Flask implementation is available in Git history.
Optional educational/export helpers inside the vaults may use Python independently; preserve their note links.
Current CSS/JS is public/static/. Keep browser assets local; no CDN, Astro or Tailwind.

Preserve 1348 UTF-8 Markdown documents, both vaults, relative .md links,
1217 legacy mappings with query parameters, old heading anchors and localStorage keys.
Code comments inside fenced blocks must not become headings. Keep CJK output safe for Windows consoles.
Never repeat the one-time folder migration. Preserve editorial: manual contents pages.

pnpm contents:refresh performs a dry run; pnpm contents:refresh --apply writes changes.
Run pnpm typecheck, pnpm contents:verify, pnpm verify and pnpm build before handoff.
Check /, /api/search.json (1348 entries), sample /doc/ pages, unknown paths 404,
legacy 308 redirects with queries, /api/search and /api/preview where affected.
See MIGRATION_NEXT.md for setup and deployment details.

Historical reports do not restore old Flask commands or superseded Python-only/no-Node rules.
